            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Darius III</strong><br>\nDarius III, originally named Artashata, was the last king of the Achaemenid Empire. He was born around 380 BCE into a noble family with a lineage that could be traced to the royal Achaemenid bloodline. Before ascending to the throne, he served as a courier and later as the royal treasurer, which gave him significant administrative experience.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Ascension to Power</strong><br>\nDarius became king of Persia in 336 BCE after the death of King Artaxerxes III and his son. His rise to power was marked by instability and challenges, as he inherited a weakened empire. This period was troubled by the declining power of the Persian central authority and frequent rebellions within the empire.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Persian Empire under Darius III</strong><br>\nThe Persian Empire during Darius III's reign was vast, stretching from the Aegean Sea to the Indus River. Despite its size, the empire was fraught with rebellious satraps and looming threats from foreign powers. Darius's rule was characterized by attempts to stabilize the empire and reform the military.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
